    {
      "id": "claim_dc327912eab042fea5343482715abd21",
      "statement": "If a target file contains more than one managed block, inject collapses them into a single block at the first occurrence's position; text outside the managed markers is preserved byte-for-byte including the file's original newline convention (\\r\\n vs \\n), which is detected and matched before writing.",
